§ `s 161(1) the court's duty to consider, and power to make, an order of prohibition`
-- (convicted or discharged on probation, the answer of s 161(1.1), the age of the person against whom the offence was committed)
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` TRUE (JUST TRUE) 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` TRUE (JUST TRUE) 17.99 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` TRUE (JUST TRUE) 18 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not "under the age of 18 years"
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` TRUE (JUST FALSE) 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an offence outside (1.1)
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` FALSE (JUST TRUE) 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither convicted nor discharged on probation
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` TRUE NOTHING 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (1.1) not established
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court may make an order of prohibition` TRUE (JUST TRUE) 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court may make an order of prohibition` TRUE (JUST TRUE) 18 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "when" gate: ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 (fork F9)
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the court may make an order of prohibition` FALSE (JUST TRUE) 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- what the order may prohibit
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` `s 161(1)(a) attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under the age of 18 years are present or can reasonably be expected to be present, or a daycare centre, schoolground, playground or community centre` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` `s 161(1)(a.1) being within two kilometres, or any other distance specified in the order, of any dwelling-house where the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides or of any other place specified in the order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` `s 161(1)(b) seeking, obtaining or continuing any employment, whether or not the employment is remunerated, or becoming or being a volunteer in a capacity, that involves being in a position of trust or authority towards persons under the age of 18 years` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` `s 161(1)(c) having any contact, including communicating by any means, with a person who is under the age of 18 years, unless the offender does so under the supervision of a person whom the court considers appropriate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` `s 161(1)(d) using the Internet or other digital network, unless the offender does so in accordance with conditions set by the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` `s 161(1) something else` EQUALS NOTHING   -- a prohibition outside the list
-- (a.1): (the answer of s 2 dwelling-house, the victim ordinarily resides there, another place specified in the order)
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the order may prohibit the offender from being near the place` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the order may prohibit the offender from being near the place` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a dwelling-house where the victim does not ordinarily reside
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the order may prohibit the offender from being near the place` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a dwelling-house
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the order may prohibit the offender from being near the place` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- any other place specified in the order
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the order may prohibit the offender from being near the place` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 "dwelling-house" not answered
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the distance in kilometres` NOTHING EQUALS 2   -- "within two kilometres"
#ASSERT `s 161(1)(a.1) the distance in kilometres` (JUST 5) EQUALS 5   -- "or any other distance specified in the order"
-- (2)
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the prohibition may be for the duration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the prohibition may be for the duration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (the prohibition is for life, the date the order is made, sentenced to imprisonment, the date of release)
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the date on which the prohibition begins` TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS NOTHING   -- for life: the text speaks of a prohibition "that is not for life"
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the date on which the prohibition begins` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)   -- not sentenced to imprisonment: only (a)
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the date on which the prohibition begins` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2030)   -- the later of (a) and (b): release is later
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the date on which the prohibition begins` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)   -- the order date is later
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the date on which the prohibition begins` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)   -- the same day
-- (3): (the court, the application is by the offender or the prosecutor, in the court's opinion desirable)
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an "if" gate on a power: NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `... TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; no application by the offender or the prosecutor: an "on application" gate of the upon kind, listed by the sweep and answered as the guide does (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05), limb by limb
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- another court and no application: the upon-kind limb decides first
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another court
-- (4)
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(4)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 4) `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 161(4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 161 test s 787(1) penalty` EQUALS `s 161 test summary penalty`
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test both`
-- the prohibition as a regulative rule (a DEONTIC value cannot be asserted on the stable binary: the traces are read)
#TRACE `s 161(4) the offender SHANT do what the order of prohibition forbids` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the offender` DOES `s 161(4) do a thing that the order of prohibition forbids` AT 3
-- (expected: BREACH: the prohibition is violated)
#TRACE `s 161(4) the offender SHANT do what the order of prohibition forbids` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)
-- (expected: the prohibition still stands, nothing has been done)

§ `s 162.2 Prohibition order: the Internet`
-- (convicted or discharged on probation, the offence)
#ASSERT `s 162.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 162.1, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 162.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(3.1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 162.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(3)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 160(3) is not 160(3.1): a "when" gate, ruling (b) (fork F9)
#ASSERT `s 162.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 162, "(1)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 162 is not 162.1
#ASSERT `s 162.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 162.1, "(1)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 162.2(2) the prohibition may be for the period` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 162.2(2) the prohibition may be for the period` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 162.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 162.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 162.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 162.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application by the offender or the prosecutor: an "on application" gate of the upon kind (the sweep of 2026-11-12; ruling (b) of 2026-11-05), limb by limb
#ASSERT `s 162.2(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 162.2(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 162.2(4)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 4) `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 162.2(4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 161 test s 787(1) penalty` EQUALS `s 161 test summary penalty`
#ASSERT `s 162.2(4) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test both`
